   the along arm on the lattice: the forward leg chases a mirror that steps away, the backward leg meets a lamp that steps toward it; the whole intervals of the accumulator and the bodies' whole steps put the lattice above or below gamma^2 by a few percent (12.3's 1.375 against 1.226 at k = 4 with one Link; here the arm is d Links and the ratio approaches the closed form as d grows)
   the across arm: the only rows that reach the co-moving mirror are the ones aimed at (a, d) with a the mirror's advance during the transit; their transit is the direction's own age at a + d, Pythagoras in the flight table's T_D (the lorentz note's Theorem 2)
   the fringe: the two arms' rows arriving together at the detector were born, or re-emitted, that many intervals apart; the wheel gives them phases that many eighths of a turn apart (the register's lamp, the turn 8); a rotation of the laboratory by 90 degrees swaps the arms and shifts the fringe by twice the difference

D. NATURE'S SCALE
   the Earth's beta = 10^-4 (30 km/s): gamma - 1 = 5.000e-09; against the cosmic background 370 km/s: 7.616e-07
   the 1887 arm, 11 m at lambda = 5.5 x 10^-7 m: the shift on a 90-degree rotation 2 d beta^2 / lambda = 0.40 fringe; observed below 0.01
   the resonators' 10^-17 against the law's 5.0e-09: 8.7 orders of magnitude (NATURE row 5b: FAIL by eight to nine)

